00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:55.580
Stop funding losing trades is a portfolio allocation rule that redirects new capital only to positions showing positive momentum rather than averaging down on under performers.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:09.940
The rule draws a direct parallel to business investment decisions. When two family members pitch ideas at Thanksgiving and one turns $10,000 into $20,000 while the other struggles, rational capital goes to the winner.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:22.560
Today's sector rotation data and makes the rule timely because financials, energy, and health care already show confirmed leadership on both daily and weekly timeframes, while solar and infrastructure lag.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:32.320
Implement it by running a weekly scan that ranks holdings by 20-day average volume and relative strength, then size new buys only in the top tier.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:42.000
The approach worked best in 2022 and 2023 when growth names rotated sharply and capital preservation mattered more than recovery bets.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.340
Risk arises when a laggard suddenly receives a volume confirmed catalyst that the screen misses.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:56.380
Investors using platforms like wealth, simple, or quest trade can set up simple relative strength alerts to automate the ranking step.

